## Non-Hoda Android deliveries (new repos, same machine)

The user also ships **non-Hoda** Android projects (games built with other AIs) to be built and published as their own new GitHub repos («توی گیت هاب یه بخش جدید اضافه کنی و اونجا بارگزاری اش کنی (مثل هُدا)»). First delivery 2026-09-06: `dnh-bit/pahpad-shahed` (native Kotlin game; current release v0.0.3, ~4.1 MB with texture assets, v2-signed with the org keystore — he renumbered the initial 1.0.0 himself, calling it 0.0.1). Full pipeline, CI-failure log, per-release workflow gotchas, the graphics/fuel iteration and the v0.0.3 external-AI graphics pass live in the `github/app-ci-delivery` skill (`SKILL.md` → «Non-Flutter Android sources → NEW repo» + `references/pahpad-shahed-case.md` + `references/game-asset-generation.md`). Key points: prefer the native Android zip over a Unity zip (scenes that must be generated inside the Unity Editor are not CI-buildable), pin Gradle via setup-gradle (runner Gradle 9 breaks AGP 8.2), verify v2 signatures with the `APK Sig Block 42` byte check rather than `META-INF/CERT.RSA`, confirm code/content presence by scanning the dex for Persian UTF-8 substrings instead of judging by APK size, update the workflow's hardcoded `tag_name` on every version bump, never adopt the external AI's own CI workflow, and **never delete/patch/annotate old releases when shipping the next version — leave them untouched («کاری به نسخه های قبل نداشته باش»)**. The prompt-vs-implement ground rule extends to games: for game debug/graphics iteration he also asks for handoff PROMPTS for his other AI («فقط پرامپت بده») rather than agent edits.

## Beta → stable promotion («نسخه جدید رو بیلد و جایگزین نسخه قبلی بکن»)

`build.yml` publishes a version as a **pre-release only when the title contains `-`** (`case "$TITLE" in *-*) PRERELEASE_FLAG="--prerelease"`), so promoting means dropping the suffix: `version: 0.2.0-beta+20` → `version: 0.2.0+21` in `pubspec.yaml` → commit + push → the run publishes a **full release** that takes the «Latest» badge. Then delete the superseded beta's release AND its tag:

```
DELETE /repos/dnh-bit/hoda/releases/{id}          → 204
DELETE /repos/dnh-bit/hoda/git/refs/tags/v0.2.0-beta%2B20  → 204
```

Notes: **the pubspec build number MUST equal the digit-concat versionCode** — `0.2.0+20` → code 20, one number. The first promotion shipped `0.2.0+21` (code 20) and the user corrected it as a mistake («دفعه قبل اشتباه کردی که نسخه رو کردی ۲۱»), ordered the +21 release deleted and a proper +20 replacement — pubspec `+N` and the digit-concat code are the same number, always. The commit message should say both things that happened (content change + promotion) since the release body is auto-generated from the version only. User's word for this is «جایگزین کن» → promote + purge in one operation (delete the beta release AND its tag, delete the +21 release AND its tag; URL-encode `+` as `%2B`), then report exactly which release/tag disappeared.

**Same-version rebuild via workflow clobber (worked 2026-09-11, istighfar-content fix) — now the preferred way to ship a fix «جایگزین فعلی» when the version must not change:** with pubspec unchanged (`0.2.0+20`) and that release+tag already existing, a normal push to `main` makes the workflow take its `gh release upload --clobber` branch — the APK asset is replaced **in place on the same release**: no second release, no tag surgery, no version bump. **But the tag does not move** — `refs/tags/vX.Y.Z+N` still points at the commit the release was first created from, so after a fix rebuild re-point it (`DELETE /git/refs/tags/v…%2B…` then `POST /git/refs` with `ref` + the new commit sha) if the release must correspond to the shipped source. Gotchas: deleting the tag makes GitHub flip the release to `draft: true` with `tag_name: untagged-<hash>` and hide the asset URL — recover with `PATCH /releases/{id} {"tag_name":"v…+N","draft":false}`, verified 2026-10-01 on 0.2.1. Verify by (a) checking the asset's `updated_at` moved on `GET /releases/{id}`, (b) downloading the fresh asset and unzipping `assets/flutter_assets/assets/hoda.db` to confirm the new content is actually inside, (c) androguard versionCode/versionName + cert SHA256. Requires the workflow to be enabled (this pattern is a legitimate build, not a surprise one).

**Verify the shipped APK with androguard, not a hand-rolled AXML parser.** `pip install androguard==3.3.5` (already present on this box) then `APK(path).get_androidversion_code() / .get_androidversion_name()` and `get_certificates_der_v2()` → `hashlib.sha256(der).hexdigest()` compared against `keytool -list -v -keystore /data/backups/hoda-upload.jks -storepass "$(cat /data/backups/.keystore_pass)" -alias hoda-upload | grep SHA256`. A match proves the release is signed with the same key as every previous one (in-place updates keep working). Parsing the binary `AndroidManifest.xml` by hand (string pool + resource map chunk walking) burned several attempts and returned nothing — don't. Reusable script: `scripts/verify_apk.py`.

## Chat-supplied single content items (between releases)

Besides docx batches the user sends ONE-OFF content straight in chat — a hadith with its source («این حدیث رو هم به دیتا بیس اضافه کن»), a dhikr to add to the ذکر section — and explicitly orders **no build and no DB-version bump**: «بدون اینکه نسخه دیتابیس رو تغییر بدی و بیلد کنی». Do exactly that: back up the DB, insert, verify, commit + push, **cancel the auto-triggered Build APK run**, leave `dbContentVersion` untouched, then report new totals and state plainly that no release was created.

- Style-match the row to the table's existing conventions (`hadiths`: arabic/farsi/source/tag/narrator/family from the 14-Ma'sumin + 9-family vocabularies; `salawat`: title/arabic/benefits/instruction/source/kind with `kind='zekr'` for ذکر entries — schema now `kind: 'salawat'|'dua'|'zekr'` — and `benefits` as a `•`-bulleted list).
- **The `salawat` table has NO `farsi` column** — a translation/معنی goes as the FIRST `•` bullet of `benefits` (UI sheet renders `benefits` → «خاصیت و توضیحات», `instruction` → «دستور عمل», `source` → «منابع»). Querying `SELECT farsi FROM salawat` throws `no such column` (bit twice in one session). Detail-sheet parsing: benefits split on `\n`, sources split on `•`.
- When the user supplies **only the Persian**, keep his wording verbatim in `farsi` and put a standard-source Arabic equivalent in `arabic` — never silently translate his text.
- **Web-search exception (user-explicit only):** «never web-search for content» governs docx batches. When he says «معنی و خواص و… آنها رو خودت از اینترنت پیدا و وارد کن» he WANTS researched benefits/instruction/source. Stay on standard sources (مفاتیحالجنان، مصباح المتهجد، بحارالأنوار، صحیح بخاری/مسلم، الکافی) and cite them in `source`. The same exception extends to **enriching existing rows on his order** («در بخش منابع و خواص ذکر استغفار جامع بازبینی کن و محتوای بهتری پیدا کن»): research via web_extract/curl on fa.wiki/tebyan/beytoote-type pages, then restructure the row as معنی-bullet + numbered property bullets each carrying its citation (آیه/روایت + مصدر) + a concrete دستور (counts, best times, conditions) + a cited منابع line. Note hawzah.net chatroom URLs 404 from this box and ravood.com is blocked — tebyan.net and beytoote.com extracts worked directly.
- **SQLite insert pitfall (cost a script run):** count the placeholders. `INSERT INTO salawat (title, arabic, benefits, instruction, source, kind) VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,'zekr')` has FIVE `?` for SIX columns — passing six params raises `ProgrammingError: statement uses 5 and there are 6 supplied`. Worse, this connection is not in autocommit: **everything a crashing script inserted before `commit()` is rolled back**, so its printed «inserted id = 354» was false (max id was still 353). Always re-run the insert with a telling-substring dup check (idempotent) and confirm with a final `SELECT COUNT(*)`.
- Batches of this shape often end with a promise of more work («بعد که آماده شدی بگو تا وصیت‌های جدید بفرستم») — record the pending batch in `references/import-batches-log.md` and open the next turn ready for it.
- **Label wording follows the user's suggestion even on UI he previously approved.** 2026-09-11: the total-reset button's label «صفر کردن شمارنده این ذکر» (set by an earlier approved pass) was ambiguous — it wiped the lifetime total too. He ordered it renamed to «صفر کردن مجموع کل» (his example text) while the newer «صفر کردن شمارندهٔ امروز» button (resetToday, disabled when today==0) stayed as-is. Two distinct reset semantics now live side by side in `salawat_screen.dart`/`salawat_store.dart`: `resetToday()` zeroes today only (total −= today), `resetTotal()` zeroes today+total. When he gives example wording, use it verbatim rather than inventing a variant.
- **Announced count ≠ file count happens — check before trusting either.** One wills docx arrived with «حدود ۲۲۰ وصیت جدید» but tables 0+1 held the SAME 120 rows already in the DB and only table 3 carried 11 new ones. Protocol: normalize names (ZWNJ→space, ي→ی, ك→ک) and set-intersect every table's names against the DB before inserting; insert only the new remainder; then report the mismatch plainly («فایل فقط ۱۱ مورد جدید داشت، نه ۲۲۰») and offer to receive the fuller file — never pad or guess. Wills dedupe key is the normalized NAME, not the text (same will can be paraphrased across doc versions).

## Reporting format

Persian, with a before→after count table, samples of inserted rows, integrity check result, and the updated .db file attached via `MEDIA:`. State explicitly whether a build did or did not run.

